{"availability":"available","full":"dangervalentine/palette-provider","name":"palette-provider","description":"🎨 Extract intelligent color palettes from images using hybrid median-cut + k-means clustering in OKLAB perceptual space. Auto-classified into dominant, supporting, and accent tiers. React · Vite · Canvas. Live demo.","category":"Design","language":"JavaScript","stars":0,"forks":0,"created":"2026-05-12T18:46:33Z","updated":"2026-09-23T19:19:41Z","branch":"main","homepage":"https://dangervalentine.github.io/palette-provider/","topics":["clustering","color-extraction","design-tools","image-processing","oklab","palette","react","vite"],"demo":"https://dangervalentine.github.io/palette-provider","color":"#25392f","ink":"#d1e5c5","lastCheckedAt":"2026-10-11T22:39:46.288Z","lastAttemptAt":"2026-10-11T22:39:46.288Z","lastAvailableAt":"2026-10-11T22:39:46.288Z","metrics":[{"at":"2026-10-11T22:39:46.288Z","stars":0,"forks":0}],"technologies":["React"],"overview":{"kind":"readme","version":1,"paragraphs":["Extract intelligent color palettes from any image","src=\"./public/palette-provider.png\" width=\"100%\" alt=\"Palette Provider title art: the wordmark beside a photograph overlaid with the samples feeding its largest color family, a palette panel in family order, and a hue-density ridge below with a peak for every family fanning into its shades.\"","Palette Provider finds the color families in an image as density peaks in the OKLAB perceptually uniform color space, so a small but distinct color (down to about 1% of the image) is not lost inside a large one. The app shows the palette next to the analysis behind it: how much of the image each family covers, where each family sits in color space, and which pixels fed it."],"features":["Color Families &mdash; Every perceptually distinct color in the image becomes a family with a faithful color and its true share, whether it covers 60% of the image or 2%.","Detail Levels &mdash; Essential (one shade per family), Balanced (up to two), or Rich (up to three). Detail adds depth within families; it never adds or removes families.","Color Limit &mdash; Show every color, or at most 8, 5, or 3 swatches. When the palette is over the limit, the closest families merge until their shades fit, so Detail decides how the swatches are spent: distinct colors…","Palette Strip &mdash; Every color in one strip, ordered by Prevalence (largest shades first) or Family (each family's shades together, families around the hue wheel). Tap a color to copy it and select its family.","Breakdown &mdash; Each family as a bar as long as its share of the image, split into its shades, with every shade's value and share."],"sourceUrl":"https://github.com/dangervalentine/palette-provider/blob/main/README.md","fingerprint":"f2a91b75951638c3bc1a637aa8dddfb881497c9dddc23d77d26e72a71fecc0c8","extractedAt":"2026-10-11T22:39:46.486Z"},"overviewCheckedAt":"2026-10-11T22:39:46.486Z","projectInsights":{"version":1,"whatItDoes":{"text":"Extract intelligent color palettes from any image","sourceUrl":"https://github.com/dangervalentine/palette-provider/blob/main/README.md"},"audience":[],"requirements":[],"fingerprint":"f2a91b75951638c3bc1a637aa8dddfb881497c9dddc23d77d26e72a71fecc0c8","sourceUrl":"https://github.com/dangervalentine/palette-provider/blob/main/README.md","checkedAt":"2026-10-11T22:39:46.486Z"},"overviewRepoUpdated":"2026-09-23T19:19:41Z","readmeSnapshot":{"version":1,"status":"saved","sourceUrl":"https://github.com/dangervalentine/palette-provider/blob/main/README.md","checkedAt":"2026-10-11T22:39:46.487Z","hash":"f2a91b75951638c3bc1a637aa8dddfb881497c9dddc23d77d26e72a71fecc0c8","originalBytes":7378,"storedBytes":7378,"truncated":false,"searchTerms":["color","family","mdash","image","shades","palette","families","oklab","detail","every","npm","strip","colors","copy","rgb","space","art","build","each","lightness","peaks","perceptually","pixel","run","share","analysis","conversions","dark","density","distinct","how"